{"agent_id":"pp3g-U4xx-exp7-t2-runner-build-zero-measured-calls-read-dd73","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-09-29T13:53:35.749256422Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4ce2b6fe-caab-4f53-9a26-d55b1dcabc0e","comment_uuid":"f5f5e325-54e5-41a0-9bfc-8c825329ab78","author":"pp3g-U4xx-exp7-t2-runner-build-zero-measured-calls-read-dd73","content":"Plan: Exp7 T2 — run_noul.py + RUNNER-PROOF.md (zero measured Jev calls, zero network).\n\n## Inputs (read-only, read via git show research/jev-phase1-565:<path>)\n- experiment7/DESIGN.md section F — the frozen builder-apparatus requirements (payload-vs-packet proof, per-record append + fsync, resume keyed by (pair_id,variant,qid), no resend, explicit+measurable retry policy, credential exclusion, freeze coverage).\n- experiment7/packet.json — the frozen 48-row Noul-only packet, sha256 c959805273627089396f9f498d6b279e068a40a0472eec8d316edb5423b2d89a, 2531933 bytes, blob 6248675f. NEVER modified. Confirmed by inspection: model is already the literal jev-1.13.0 (no placeholder, unlike exp6), qid=sufficiency, type=noul, NO criteria key, one question per request, request_sha256 == sha256(json.dumps(request,ensure_ascii=False,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':'))) for 48/48 rows.\n- experiment6/AMENDMENT-2.md — the three proven harness/run_jev.py defects to avoid inheriting.\n- phase2/harness/run_jev.py — READ ONLY, to identify those three defects and to cross-check the transport/parse/classify behaviour. NOT reused as the runner and NOT imported at run time.\n- phase1/harness/common.py + phase1/followup-03/harness/{run_ops.py,jev_ratelimit_probe.py} — the proven retry/backoff/curl-transport shapes and the recorded 403/429 incident.\n\n## Outputs (exactly 2 paths)\n1. experiment7/run_noul.py — stdlib-only, self-contained executor for the 48 frozen rows. Subcommands: plan | proof | run | verify.\n2. experiment7/RUNNER-PROOF.md — GENERATED by 'proof' from computed values (never transcribed, so it cannot drift), same discipline as PACKET-CHECK.md.\n\n## Runner design decisions\n- SELF-CONTAINED, no harness import. Reason: DESIGN section F requires retry-after honour, per-record attempt counters and a named credential location, none of which run_jev.post/parse_noul/load_key provide; and the phase2/harness tree is not present in this worktree (different branch, another worktree), so a runtime import would make the runner non-runnable where the packet is. Cost of reimplementation is met by check P-X: a zero-spend parity check that extracts the frozen harness blobs from git at PINNED blob sha1s and compares classify() and parse_noul() against this runner's implementations on a fixture corpus, so divergence is detected rather than assumed away.\n- ZERO SUBSTITUTION. Unlike exp6, the packet already carries the literal jev-1.13.0, so request bytes are taken verbatim: no model placeholder is filled, no state is rendered, no question is generated. That structurally forecloses AMENDMENT-2 defect 1 (decisive fact dropped) and defect 2 (one-size option plan) — the per-row question comes from the packet, and a Noul row has no option set at all.\n- BYTES, NOT OBJECTS. One pinned canonical serialiser (sort_keys, compact separators, ensure_ascii=False) defines the wire body; request_hash = sha256 of exactly those bytes; the same serialiser is how the packet's own request_sha256 was computed, so the runner asserts request_hash == packet.request_sha256 for all 48 rows. The body is written to a 0700 temp file, read back, and the readback hash re-checked before curl is invoked, so 'request_hash of the exact body sent' is mechanical.\n- AMENDMENT-2 defect 3 closed: append + fsync per record to results/exec.jsonl (line-buffered append, flush, os.fsync), never a post-loop write. Resume keyed by the specified stable (pair_id, variant, qid), with a documented strengthening: a key present on disk whose request_hash differs from the planned one ABORTS the run rather than being skipped, because keying on the triple alone would mask a packet that moved under the runner.\n- Retry policy, frozen and measurable: max_attempts 3; fixed no-jitter backoff (1,2,4)s (phase-1 precedent, keeps runs comparable); retryable = network/timeout/429/5xx; non-retryable = other 4xx, parse error, and response-model mismatch (a contract violation is a finding, not a transient fault). 429 honours Retry-After (delta-seconds AND HTTP-date, case-insensitive, last header block wins) clamped to a recorded ceiling; absence of the header falls back to the schedule. Per record: attempt (final), retries, and a retry_history list of {attempt, http_status, typed_error, retry_after_s, slept_s, wait_source}, so the counters are observable in the artifact, not just on stdout.\n- Response-model assertion per record (PRIMATIVES section 7): raw_response.model must equal jev-1.13.0; a mismatch is a terminal typed_error model_mismatch, never silently accepted.\n- Credential: resolved ONLY from a named location — env var TYPESAFE_API_KEY or an explicit --credential-file PATH. Only the LABEL is ever recorded. The value reaches curl on stdin via --config - (never argv, never a file, never an artifact, never an exception message); a credential containing a quote/backslash/newline is refused rather than mangled (the phase-2 curl-config defect).\n- Zero-spend is MECHANICAL: proof/plan/verify install a socket blocker at run time (socket.socket subclass refusing instantiation, plus create_connection/create_server/socketpair/getaddrinfo/gethostbyname), so the proof cannot accidentally spend. 'run' is the only subcommand that can send, and it refuses to run unless every gate passes first.\n\n## How RUNNER-PROOF.md earns its claims (all zero-spend, all computed)\n1. Exact outgoing body equality vs the frozen packet for all 48 rows, on three independent axes: (a) byte identity of the canonical body against the packet row re-serialised from the packet file; (b) a recursive structural comparison that never touches the serialiser, so a serialiser bug cannot round-trip its own output; (c) request_hash == packet.request_sha256 == re-hash of the bytes actually staged in the temp file. Plus the schema gates that must hold before a byte is staged (model/qid/type/no-criteria/one-question/state-vs-exp6 hash).\n2. Planned cardinality 48, re-derived by grouping the plan, not read from a declared count; 24 pair_ids x {U,A}; 48 distinct resume keys; pair-completeness and no-orphan checks.\n3. Resume and no-resend logic proven with SYNTHETIC LOCAL FIXTURES in a temp dir: (a) empty results file -> 48 to send; (b) 3 completed records -> exactly those 3 skipped and 45 queued, and the skipped set is the resume key set; (c) a record carrying a retryable error with attempts remaining is NOT treated as complete; (d) a record with a terminal non-retryable error IS complete; (e) a duplicate key on disk is a corruption and aborts; (f) a key on disk with a different request_hash aborts; (g) resume is a pure function of the file — two loads of the same file give the same skip set; (h) interrupting a synthetic send loop and re-running sends nothing twice.\n4. Retry counters observable: synthetic transport fixtures drive 429-then-200, 500-then-500-then-200, 429 with Retry-After (delta-seconds), 429 with Retry-After (HTTP-date), 429 with no header, 400 (no retry), parse error (no retry), network error then 200 — asserting the exact attempt count, retry count, per-attempt retry_history entries, and the honoured wait. Sleep is injected, so the proof is instant and deterministic.\n5. Credential hygiene: the runner's own source is scanned to prove no credential value can reach an artifact (no key in argv, no key in any record, no key in any exception path); the credential resolver is exercised against a synthetic secret in a temp file and the result is proven absent from the record it would produce.\n6. Freeze coverage: this runner, packet.json, DESIGN.md, PRIMATIVES.md, reuse_check.json and the read-only experiment6 packet are re-hashed and pinned; the exp6 tree is proven unmodified.\n7. What the harness did NOT get: a check that the runner never renders state or questions (no import of represent/run_jev in the send path, asserted from the module AST) and never uses a question plan.\n\n## Constraints honoured\nZERO measured Jev calls and ZERO network calls of any kind. Nothing under experiment6/ touched; packet.json, build_packet.py, PACKET-CHECK.md, DESIGN.md, PRIMATIVES.md, reuse_check.json all read-only. No other file created or modified. Commit contains exactly the 2 new paths on #574.\n\n## Certainty\nPlan is evidence-based, not merely assumed: the packet's request_sha256 recipe was re-derived and verified 48/48, so the body-equality check rests on a recipe that is known to match the frozen artifact. NOT-TESTED and explicitly NOT claimed: that jev-1.13.0 accepts this Noul body, that the credential location resolves on this machine, what the model would answer, the observed Retry-After header shape from the live endpoint (the parser accepts both legal forms and the recorded evidence is what the phase-1 probes actually saw), and any behavioural property of Jev. Environment caveat as before: the phase2 tree lives on research/jev-phase1-565 (another worktree), so the runner resolves packet.json by disk-then-git-show and the proof run here uses the git fallback.","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:53:35.741905085Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:V37X/kri6wzcRXUTR9t9HUmszrGVryqOUDHIx1aTeKI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgJRw9xkr2U2V1BunmJ1Ab9hPF9YIwEGqvmgPhIxUm6nIAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAKB78Q9slvnUcm4kxshGx5kBh69D85ompOegeUBjqyhP5yoydU/YOho6rpIHczKCOYey4td4IO1HbQru5Cha2AA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:V37X/kri6wzcRXUTR9t9HUmszrGVryqOUDHIx1aTeKI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgJRw9xkr2U2V1BunmJ1Ab9hPF9YIwEGqvmgPhIxUm6nIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOWopPkk64ZRH5EL5vgMJ3VJZWxPuo3lbbHVWZKywp1AaC2AdXKCE/Qcd0B0SVZf07Qy1hVmiApZ9GrqPUa22gs="}
